-- Arzno (Rifts World Book 28): Imitator power armor and TW vehicles
-- 12 vehicle rows, with 70 locations and 59 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~245-arzno-vehicles.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.
-- Rifts World Book 28: Arzno, printed 91-109: the five Imitator power armors
-- (series rules 89-90) and seven TW aircraft and ground vehicles; extracted off
-- renders, checked by book-reconcile. Techno-Wizard features are stored as
-- vehicle_weapons entries whose note says they are features. Cost is the
-- cheapest printed Arzno price; the Whirlybird's is printed "460,00" and is
-- stored NULL.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('tw-jackrabbit-power-armor', 'TW Jackrabbit Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running (Normal): 40 mph (64 km) in a normal, human style of running upright; tires the pilot at 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Jackrabbit Run (voice command or key pad code in the left forearm): loping, zigzag pattern with random long leaps, sharp turns, frequent dodging. Maximum speed 65 mph (104 km), increased by 30% (85 mph/136 km) when the light rail gun is stowed and the operator runs (lopes) on all fours. Leaping: 20 feet (6.1 m) high and 40 feet (12.2 m) across; increase height and distance by 30% with a Jackrabbit running start.', 'Not possible.', 'Normal Spd and -5% on skill performance. Can survive underwater depths of up to 400 feet (122 m).', 'Already a specialty item; size is totally customizable. Add 30% to cost if over 8 feet (2.4 m) tall.', '110 lbs (49.5 kg)', 135, 1, NULL, 1200000, 'Market Price: 1.2 million credits at Arzno. Exclusively sold by Arzno, but 2.5 million to 3.2 million credits when the Black Market gets its hands on one. Optional forearm weapon costs an extra 15,000-25,000 credits.', 'Light, very fast ground suit inspired by the Triax Terrain Hopper: 40 mph normal running, 65-85 mph in zigzag Jackrabbit mode, huge leaps and automatic dodges, and a TW overdrive that doubles the speed. Light rail gun (silver or conventional rounds) plus optional forearm weapon; at least a third of buyers choose it for its reputed luck, though its designers say it is not magical. Model: Arzno TWA-1230JR Jackrabbit Power Armor. Base model for light, quick ground armor. Full environmental TW power armor. P.S.: +6 to the P.S. of the pilot and is equal to Bionic/Augmented P.S. Power system: Nuclear or TW generator. P.P.E. battery: 200 points to activate the TW features without having to draw upon the pilot''s own P.P.E. reserve. Once depleted, can be recharged by a Techno-Wizard, ley line or the magical feature may be activated by the operator''s own P.P.E. or I.S.P. Bonuses: +1 on initiative, +3 to automatic dodge (dodging does not use up a melee attack/action; +7 to automatic dodge when running on all fours), +2 to roll with impact, +10% to Gymnastics skill percentiles (if the pilot has it); zero to full speed in 3 seconds (uses up one melee attack/action), stop on a dime. All in addition to usual Power Armor combat bonuses for Basic or Elite level skills. One of the five Arzno Imitator series suits (series rules printed 89-90): full environmental Techno-Wizard power armor sold by A.W.M.; each TW feature costs N P.P.E. or 2N I.S.P. and draws on the TW P.P.E. Battery (tw-ppe-battery).', 'Rifts World Book 28: Arzno - Vampire Incursion p.91-92'),
  ('tw-lonewolf-power-armor', 'TW Lonewolf Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, '1. Enhanced Speed - Running: 75 mph (120 km) in a normal, human-style of running upright; tires the pilot at 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 16 feet (4.9 m) high and 22 feet (6.7 m) across; increase by 20% with a running start.', 'Not possible.', 'Double the operator''s normal swimming speed; can survive underwater depths of up to 500 feet (152 m).', 'Already a specialty item; size is totally customizable. Add 30% to cost if over 8 feet (2.4 m) tall.', '155 lbs (69.8 kg)', 200, 1, NULL, 1500000, 'Market Price: 1.5 million credits at Arzno. Exclusively sold by Arzno, but 2.8 million to 5 million credits when the Black Market gets its hands on one, more if loaded down with weapons.', 'All-purpose medium infantry suit: 200 M.D.C. main body, 75 mph running, a medium rail gun firing silver or M.D. rounds. TW features are See Invisible, a force shield and a Mystic Assault of boosted punches and energy blasts. Model: Arzno TWA-1240LW Lonewolf Power Armor. ''basically an all-purpose infantry unit'' (series text: base model for medium infantry ground armor). P.S.: Robotic P.S. of 24. Power system: Nuclear or TW generator. P.P.E. battery: 200 points to activate the TW features. Bonuses: +1 on initiative, +1 to strike, parry, and dodge, +1 to disarm, +2 to pull punch; zero to full speed in 6 seconds (uses up two melee actions), stop on a dime. In addition to usual Power Armor Combat bonuses for Basic or Elite. Helmet in two styles: wolf-like, or a pug-version reminiscent of a lion headdress (pilot looks through a tinted plate in the open mouth); body styling similar to the Thunderbird minus wings and protruding chest. One of the five Arzno Imitator series suits (series rules printed 89-90): full environmental Techno-Wizard power armor sold by A.W.M.; each TW feature costs N P.P.E. or 2N I.S.P. and draws on the TW P.P.E. Battery (tw-ppe-battery).', 'Rifts World Book 28: Arzno - Vampire Incursion p.92-93'),
  ('tw-raging-bull-power-armor', 'TW Raging Bull Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (80 km) in a normal, human style of running upright; 20% of normal fatigue rate. (TW Raging Bull feature increases speed by 50%.) Leaping: 8 feet (2.4 m) high and 15 feet (4.6 m) across; increase by 20% with a running start.', 'Not possible.', 'Double the operator''s normal swimming speed; can survive underwater depths of up to 1200 feet (366 m). (Printed at top of the right column of folio 94.)', 'Already a specialty item; size is totally customizable. Add 50% to cost if over 8 feet (2.4 m) tall.', '430 lbs (193.5 kg)', 385, 1, NULL, 2000000, 'Market Price: 2 million credits at Arzno. Exclusively sold by Arzno, but 4 to 5 million credits when the Black Market gets its hands on one, more if loaded down with weapons.', 'Heavy, strong ground suit (385 M.D.C. main body, Robotic P.S. 30) with a heavy rail gun. TW features: Superhuman Strength, and a berserk Raging Bull mode adding 60 M.D.C. and extra attacks at the cost of bloodlust and a post-rage penalty. Poor mobility. Model: Arzno TWA-1250RB Raging Bull Power Armor. Also known as ''the Minotaur'' armor; heavy armor and brute strength (series text: base for bears, rhinos and similar big, bulky armor). P.S.: Robotic P.S. of 30. Power system: Nuclear or TW generator. P.P.E. battery: 200 points to activate the TW features. Mobility: Poor mobility; -20% to climb, prowl, swim, or perform acrobatics and similar physical skills. Bonuses: +1 to strike and parry, +2 to pull punch; zero to full speed in 6 seconds (uses up two melee actions), stop on a dime. In addition to usual Power Armor Combat bonuses. TW Raging Bull bonuses (while active): +60 M.D.C. to armor (damage comes off this first), +2 attacks per melee round, +2 on initiative, +2 to strike, +1 to parry, does not fatigue, pain not felt, +1 on all saving throws for the duration, impervious to mind control, Horror Factor, possession, drugs, and psionic and magic illusions. Bovine head with horns and a nose ring; hydraulics and hoses visible; eyes glow red when TW features run. One of the five Arzno Imitator series suits (series rules printed 89-90): full environmental Techno-Wizard power armor sold by A.W.M.; each TW feature costs N P.P.E. or 2N I.S.P. and draws on the TW P.P.E. Battery (tw-ppe-battery).', 'Rifts World Book 28: Arzno - Vampire Incursion p.93-95'),
  ('tw-thunderbird-power-armor', 'TW Thunderbird Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (80 km) in a normal, human-style of running upright; 20% of normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 10 feet (3 m) high and 15 feet (4.6 m) across without engaging the flight system; increase by 10% with a running start.', 'See TW Wing Pack: up to 240 mph (380 km), maximum altitude 10,000 feet (3,050 m); max speed in a few seconds (one attack); silent flight.', 'Double the operator''s normal swimming speed; can survive underwater depths of up to 1200 feet (366 m).', 'Already a specialty item; size is totally customizable. Add 50% to cost if over 8 feet (2.4 m) tall.', '430 lbs (193.5 kg)', 220, 1, NULL, 2500000, 'Market Price: 2.5 million credits, created and sold exclusively by Arzno, but 5 to 7 million credits when the Black Market gets its hands on one, more if loaded down with extra weapons.', 'Basic flying suit of the series (SAMAS-like, four wings) flying 240 mph to 10,000 feet on a TW wing pack. Carries a laser rifle with grenade launcher, 20 wing mini-missiles and eight forearm blades; TW features add long-range optics with target lock-on and an outdoor-only call-lightning artillery attack. Model: Arzno TWA-1260TB Thunderbird Power Armor. ''the basic aerial power armor in the Imitator series'' (series text: base model for flying power armor). P.S.: Robotic P.S. of 24. Power system: TW generator only! P.P.E. battery: 200 points to activate the TW features. Mobility: Excellent aerial mobility, but -5% to climb, -15% to swim or perform gymnastics. Bonuses: +1 on initiative, +1 to strike, +2 to dodge when airborne, +1 to disarm, +1 to pull punch; zero to full speed in 6 seconds (two melee actions), stop on a dime. In addition to usual Power Armor Combat bonuses. Eagle Eye Optics lock-on: +3 to strike on an Aimed or Called Shot, +1 on a burst or other shooting. Eagle Eye Optics (TW feature 2): see a sign or identify a raven up to three miles (4.8 km) away, Nightvision, See the Invisible up to 2000 feet (610 m), zoom up to 30x with target lock (target not faster than 100 mph/160 km); while locked: tunnel vision, no initiative, no bonuses to strike, parry, dodge, -10 to parry or dodge incoming attacks. Chest searchlight. Silent flight. *Items marked by a single asterisk are small, obscured and/or difficult to strike unless a "Called Shot" is made, and even then the shooter is -4 to strike. Destroying one wing reduces the bonus to dodge by -1 and reduces speed by 10%. Destroying two wings reduces dodge bonuses to zero and speed by 50%. Destroying three wings makes the power armor limp along at a mere 10% of its usual speed and altitude, and all remaining combat bonuses, other than those from W.P. skills, are reduced to only +1. One of the five Arzno Imitator series suits (series rules printed 89-90): full environmental Techno-Wizard power armor sold by A.W.M.; each TW feature costs N P.P.E. or 2N I.S.P. and draws on the TW P.P.E. Battery (tw-ppe-battery).', 'Rifts World Book 28: Arzno - Vampire Incursion p.95-98'),
  ('tw-guardian-angel-power-armor', 'TW Guardian Angel Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 40 mph (64 km) in a normal, human style of running upright; 20% of normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 10 feet (3 m) high and 15 feet (4.6 m) across without engaging the flight system; increase by 10% with a running start.', 'TW Angelic Wings: 50 mph (80 km), and may hover stationary.', 'Double the operator''s normal swimming speed; can survive underwater depths of up to 1200 feet (366 m).', 'Already a specialty item; size is totally customizable. Add 50% to cost if over 8 feet (2.4 m) tall.', '220 lbs (99 kg)', 170, 1, NULL, 3000000, 'Market Price: 3 million credits at Arzno. Exclusively sold by Arzno, but 6-9 million credits when the Black Market can get its hands on one.', 'Rescue and medical flyer: healing touch, Sense Evil / turn dead / hold-off-vampires, glowing magic wings with an Awe Factor, and a magic force field (80 M.D.C.), no built-in weapons. Worn by A.M.C. chaplains and medics, vampire hunters and Body Fixers. Model: Arzno TWA-1270GA Guardian Angel Power Armor. Rescue and medical aerial power armor (series text: aerial power armor, rescue and medical armor). P.S.: Robotic P.S. of 22. Power system: TW generator only! P.P.E. battery: 200 points. Mobility: Very good mobility, but -5% to climb, swim, prowl and similar physical skills. Bonuses: +2 to dodge when airborne, +1 to pull punch, +2 to roll with impact; zero to full speed in 6 seconds (two melee actions), stop on a dime. In addition to usual Power Armor Combat bonuses. Body: cross between the Light TW Body Armor and the Thunderbird minus wings; light blue/gray/white/gold/silver with a large red cross on the chest and smaller crosses on knees, shoulder plates, helmet; helmet like the Light TW body armor. One of the five Arzno Imitator series suits (series rules printed 89-90): full environmental Techno-Wizard power armor sold by A.W.M.; each TW feature costs N P.P.E. or 2N I.S.P. and draws on the TW P.P.E. Battery (tw-ppe-battery).', 'Rifts World Book 28: Arzno - Vampire Incursion p.98-99'),
  ('tw-grinning-gunship', 'TW Grinning Gunship', 'rifts', 'vehicle', '2 or 3; one pilot, one copilot/gunner/communications, one optional door gunner. Can carry an additional 4-5 soldiers or 2 power armor troopers.', NULL, NULL, '80 mph (128 km), or double on a ley line', NULL, '60 feet (18.3 m) long, 10 feet (3.0 m) wide, and 17 feet (5.2 m) tall. Rotor blades are 25 feet (7.6 m) long each, so spin in a 50 foot (15.2 m) circle.', '10 tons fully loaded', 110, 1, NULL, 2400000, 'Basic unit requiring P.P.E. every time it is used: 2.4 million credits in Arzno; powered by an additional P.P.E. Battery: 2.8 million; powered by a TW generator (with built-in P.P.E. Battery): 4.9 million. Sells for two or three times that amount on the Black Market. (Intro: purchased by the A.M.C. from the Black Market; unique in Arzno; A.M.C. has a half dozen. TW Features note: reduce cost by two million without the TW generator.)', 'A TW-powered combat helicopter bought by the A.M.C. from the Black Market and fitted with a 200 M.D.C. magic force field. It carries a pilot, copilot and optional door gunner plus 4-5 soldiers, and is armed with a nose rail gun and a 48-mini-missile arm. Model: Arzno TWV-4100 Gunship. Vehicle type: Helicopter. Cargo: Primarily a combat and transport vehicle, the Gunship isn''t well suited for hauling anything more than a few soldiers and their gear. A weapon rack can hold a dozen energy rifles and a few dozen E-Clips or other small items, and a pair of small storage closets can hold three suits of armor each. Storage drawers under the pilot and copilot seats hold a grand total of 4 cubic feet (0.1 cubic meters) each. If no troops are carried, the chopper can carry about a ton of materials in the space typically reserved for soldiers and gunners. Total available space would be a bay 8 feet (2.4 m) wide, 10 feet (3.0 m) tall, and 20 feet (6.1 m) long. Power system: Varies. A TW generator will power the vehicle for 20 years, twice that if used infrequently. A TW battery with 200 P.P.E. offers limited power (roughly 16 hours of fly time), or the vehicle can be set up to function for two hours every time the pilot (or someone) pumps 25 P.P.E. (or 50 I.S.P.) into it. Built-in P.P.E. Battery (Standard): A built-in reserve holds 100 P.P.E., enough for an additional 8 hours of flight time, but it is specifically intended to power the special TW Features. The vehicle and TW features may also run directly off the operator''s own P.P.E. or I.S.P. Currently only the magic force field and TW generator are standard on the vehicle, reduce cost by two million without the TW generator.', 'Rifts World Book 28: Arzno - Vampire Incursion p.99-102'),
  ('tw-kamikaze-fighter', 'TW "Kamikaze" Fighter', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot.', NULL, NULL, '250 mph (400 km), or 500 mph (800 km) on a ley line Minimum speed is about 60 mph (96 km) without losing altitude.', NULL, '18 feet (5.4 m) long, 4 feet (1.2 m) wide, 4 feet (1.2 m) tall, and a wingspan of 18 feet (5.4 m).', '1,500 lbs (675 kg)', 100, 1, NULL, 2600000, 'Basic unit requiring P.P.E. every time it is used: 2.6 million credits in Arzno; powered by an additional P.P.E. Battery: 3 million; powered by a TW generator (with built-in P.P.E. Battery): 5.1 million. Sells for two or three times that amount on the Black Market. Note: The 4500B "bomber" would cost an extra million for its missile and bomb carry capabilities plus the cost of ordnance. (The 4500B is a planned second generation, none produced.)', 'A one-seat propeller fighter built from salvaged pre-Rifts aircraft with magical propulsion, used for infantry support, escort and attacks on aircraft and structures. It has a nose TK machine-gun, wing-mounted missiles and an optional TW-VTOL assist; a bomber 4500B variant is described but not produced. Model: Arzno TWV-4500A Fighter. Vehicle type: Airplane. Cargo: Virtually none; a small backpack under the seat. Power system: Varies. A TW generator will power the vehicle for 20 years, twice that if used infrequently. A TW battery with 200 P.P.E. offers limited power (roughly 16 hours of fly time), or the vehicle can be set up to function for two hours every time the pilot (or someone) pumps 25 P.P.E. (or 50 I.S.P.) into it. Built-in P.P.E. Battery (Standard): A built-in reserve holds 100 P.P.E., enough for an additional 8 hours of flight time, but it is specifically intended to power the special TW Features. The vehicle and TW features may also run directly off the operator''s own P.P.E. or I.S.P. Stats for the 4500B model are in parentheses. No section headed Techno-Wizard Features; the TW-VTOL is listed as Weapon Systems item 3 Additional Systems. Built-in 100 P.P.E. battery is specifically intended to power the special TW Features.', 'Rifts World Book 28: Arzno - Vampire Incursion p.101-102'),
  ('tw-whirlybird-personal-helicopter', 'TW "Whirlybird" Personal Helicopter', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot.', NULL, NULL, '100 mph (161 km), or double on a ley line Can move in any direction or even hover.', NULL, '10 feet (3.0 m) long, 4 feet (1.2 m) wide, and 8 feet (2.4 m) tall. Rotor blades are 6 feet (1.8 m) long each, so spin in a 12 feet (3.7 m) diameter. (Intro: tail extends six feet behind the cockpit; three main blades.)', '800 pounds (363 kg)', 115, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Basic unit requiring P.P.E. every time it is used: 460,00 credits in Arzno [printed 460,00, one digit short, confirmed on the render]; powered by an additional P.P.E. Battery: 850,000; powered by a TW generator (with built-in P.P.E. Battery): 2.8 million (a similar model from Stormspire sells for 3.6 million). Sells for two or three times that amount on the Black Market. Now mass produced by A.W.M.', 'A one-seat egg-cockpit personal helicopter, now mass produced by A.W.M. and used for scouting, personal travel and combat, powered entirely by P.P.E. The buyer chooses any two of eight optional systems: guns, laser, missiles, fire blaster, vampire-killing light, comm package, adhesion skids or extra carrying capacity. Model: Arzno TWV-4000 Personal Helicopter. Vehicle type: Helicopter. Cargo: 10 cubic feet (0.3 cubic meters) Power system: Varies. A TW generator will power the vehicle for 20 years, twice that if used infrequently. A TW battery with 200 P.P.E. offers limited power (roughly 16 hours of fly time), or the vehicle can be set up to function for two hours every time the pilot (or someone) pumps 25 P.P.E. (or 50 I.S.P.) into it. Built-in P.P.E. Battery (Standard): A built-in reserve holds 100 P.P.E., enough for an additional 8 hours of flight time, but it is specifically intended to power the special TW Features. The vehicle and TW features may also run directly off the operator''s own P.P.E. or I.S.P. Special Features: This vehicle is often used solely for transport or reconnaissance and does not need any advanced systems. However, this versatile craft is a fully capable military machine and can be outfitted with any two of the following systems: No section headed Techno-Wizard Features. Optional systems 1-8 are printed under Special Features (choose any two). Item 4 is labeled TW; item 7 is labeled TW Carpet of Adhesion Skids.', 'Rifts World Book 28: Arzno - Vampire Incursion p.102-104'),
  ('tw-sandstorm-hover-craft', 'TW Sandstorm Hover Craft', 'rifts', 'vehicle', '1 pilot, 1 co-pilot/gunner, up to 2 passengers (may double as additional gunners).', NULL, '110 mph (176 km) max. Cruising speed is closer to 60 mph (97 km).', 'Maximum elevation above the surface is 3 feet (0.9 m) Can perform jumps and free falls similar to hovercycles.', 'Intro: functions in swamps and riding over water (no speed printed)', '12 feet (3.6 m) long, 8 feet (2.4 m) wide, and 6 feet (1.8 m) tall.', '2 tons', 140, 1, NULL, 850000, 'Basic unit requiring P.P.E. every time it is used: 850,000 credits in Arzno; powered by an additional P.P.E. Battery: 1.2 million; powered by a TW generator (with built-in P.P.E. Battery): 3.6 million. Sells for two or three times that amount on the Black Market. Purchasing without the force field reduces the cost by one million credits.', 'An open-frame, three-fan hover platform, part of the Arzno arsenal and used by the Mercenary Corps, that reaches 110 mph at up to 3 feet off the ground and works over sand, swamp and water. It carries four, comes standard with an 80 M.D.C. force field, and is armed with a shotgun, a mini-missile launcher, a cross-casting headlight and a dust-cloud screen. Model: Arzno TWV-2100 Hover Craft. Vehicle type: Hover Craft. Cargo: 10 cubic feet (0.3 cubic meters) storage space, plus whatever can be stowed on the deck. Power system: Varies. A TW generator will power the vehicle for 20 years, twice that if used infrequently. A TW battery with 200 P.P.E. offers limited power (roughly 20 hours of constant use), or the vehicle can be set up to function for one hour every time the pilot (or someone) pumps 10 P.P.E. (or 20 I.S.P.) into it. Built-in P.P.E. Battery (Standard): A built-in reserve holds 100 P.P.E., enough for an additional 10 hours of drive time, but it is specifically intended to power the special TW Features. The vehicle and TW features may also run directly off the operator''s own P.P.E. or I.S.P.', 'Rifts World Book 28: Arzno - Vampire Incursion p.104-105'),
  ('tw-cliff-rider-personal-atv', 'TW "Cliff Rider" Personal ATV', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot; one passenger can ride behind the driver, but is uncomfortable on long trips.', NULL, '65 mph (104 km) top speed on the ground; about 40-45 mph (64-72 km) going up cliff facings, canyon walls and the sides or ceilings of buildings.', NULL, NULL, 'Height: 4 feet, 2 inches (1.3 m); Width: 4 feet (1.2 m); Length: 6 feet, 3 inches (1.9 m)', '550 pounds (248 kg)', 85, 1, NULL, 350000, 'Basic unit requiring P.P.E. every time it is used: 350,000 credits in Arzno; powered by an additional P.P.E. Battery: 750,000 credits; powered by a TW generator (with built-in P.P.E. Battery): 3.5 million. Sells for two or three times that amount on the Black Market. TW Force Field add-on: extra one million credits.', 'A one-seat (plus one passenger) mystically powered four-wheeled ATV from A.W.M. that can climb sheer walls and drive along ceilings via its standard Cliff Rider feature. It has no standard weapons and is popular with the A.M.C., ranchers and thrill-seekers. Model: Arzno TWV-2000 ATV. Vehicle type: All-Terrain Vehicle; uses Pilot: Motorcycle. Cargo: Can carry 1,000 pounds (450 kg) in riders and gear, with storage space on a rack in the back, or tied elsewhere on the vehicle. The Cliff Rider can tow an additional 1,000 pounds (450 kg). Power system: Varies. A TW generator will power the vehicle for 20 years, twice that if used infrequently. A TW battery with 200 P.P.E. offers limited power (roughly 16 hours of constant use), or the vehicle can be set up to function for two hours every time the pilot (or someone) pumps 25 P.P.E. (or 50 I.S.P.) into it. Built-in P.P.E. Battery (Standard): A built-in reserve holds 100 P.P.E., enough for an additional eight hours of drive time, but it is specifically intended to power the special TW Features. The vehicle and TW features may also run directly off the operator''s own P.P.E. or I.S.P. Bonuses: Even when the Cliff Rider feature is not engaged, the ATV gets extremely good traction and holds to the road well, reducing piloting skill penalties for stunt driving by half. None standard, but a light weapon could be mounted forward on the vehicle for additional cost. Only its P.P.E. power supply and trademark wall-climbing ability are standard. The military and wealthy buyers sometimes add the TW Force Field to the ATV (provides 80 M.D.C. and protects drive and vehicle) for an extra one million credits.', 'Rifts World Book 28: Arzno - Vampire Incursion p.106-107'),
  ('tw-rover-dune-buggy', 'TW "Rover" Dune Buggy', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot and three passengers (one sitting "shotgun," and two facing the rear).', NULL, '120 mph (192 km) top speed on just about any level surface including sand, snow, and paved roads. Accelerates and brakes within incredibly short distances.', NULL, NULL, 'Height: 5 feet, 9 inches (1.8 m); Width: 8 feet (2.4 m); Length: 12 feet (3.7 m)', '1150 pounds (518 kg)', 135, 1, NULL, 90000, 'Basic unit requiring P.P.E. every time it is used: 90,000 credits in Arzno; powered by an additional P.P.E. Battery: 450,000 credits; powered by a TW generator (with built-in P.P.E. Battery): 2.3 million. Sells for two or three times that amount on the Black Market. Simplicity and low cost are named as appeals.', 'A light open-frame dune buggy with almost no armor, favored by speed seekers and used by the Arzno Mercenary Corps as nimble support. It seats four, tops out at 120 mph, is cheap and simple to drive, and carries a swivel-mounted light rail gun or laser up front. Model: Arzno TWV-2500 Dune Buggy. Vehicle type: Automobile, or may use any basic ground vehicle skill at -5% to operate the dune buggy due to its simple controls. Cargo: Can carry the pilot, the three passengers, and enough basic equipment for each. Space is limited to cargo boxes built underneath the seats, and is not meant for heavy-duty hauling. Power system: Varies. A TW generator will power the vehicle for 20 years, twice that if used infrequently. A TW battery with 200 P.P.E. offers limited power (roughly 40 hours of constant use), or the vehicle can be set up to function four hours every time the pilot (or someone) pumps 5 P.P.E. (or 10 I.S.P.) into it. Built-in P.P.E. Battery: Optional for an additional cost of 225,000 credits, a built-in TW P.P.E. Battery holding a reserve of 100 P.P.E. can be added. This is enough for an additional 20 hours of drive time, but is seldom purchased unless TW Features are added; the Dune Buggy doesn''t usually come with TW features. Bonuses: +1 to dodge due to quickness, and good acceleration and braking response. The Rover typically includes a light rail gun mounted on a swivel in the front of the vehicle, along with the spotlight. Extremely customizable; often equipped with more weapons for use by the passengers. Techno-Wizard Features: None standard, other than the power system. As many as three TW features may be added for an additional cost, but most people don''t bother, although one third of the military vehicles in the A.M.C. have the TW Force Field (80 M.D.C.) and the P.P.E. Battery to power it.', 'Rifts World Book 28: Arzno - Vampire Incursion p.107-108'),
  ('tw-sand-ranger-combat-truck', 'TW "Sand Ranger" Combat Truck', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot and two passengers in the cab, and five passengers in the bed (as many as eight passengers in the bed if the mounted weapon is removed).', NULL, '100 mph (160 km) is top speed, half on loose sand, no speed impediment in the rocky deserts.', NULL, NULL, 'Height: 6 feet, 11 inches (2.1 m); Width: 8 feet (2.4 m); Length: 18 feet (5.5 m)', '3,200 pounds (1,440 kg)', 212, 1, NULL, 265000, 'Basic unit requiring P.P.E. every time it is used: 265,000 credits in Arzno; powered by an additional P.P.E. Battery: 990,000 credits; powered by a TW generator (with built-in P.P.E. Battery): 3.2 million. Sells for two or three times that amount on the Black Market. Appeals named: simplicity, ease of construction, comparatively low cost.', 'A pickup-style armored truck with an enclosed cab and open bed, used by the Arzno military and by mercenaries as a combined assault vehicle and troop carrier. It hauls about 5,000 lbs, tops out at 100 mph, and mounts forward twin plasma cannons plus a swiveling heavy weapon in the bed. Model: Arzno TWV-2800 Combat Truck. Vehicle type: All-Purpose Vehicle (use Pilot: Automobile skill). Cargo: Can carry roughly 5,000 pounds (2250 kg) and tow an additional 6,000 pounds (2,700 kg). Power system: Varies. A TW generator will power the vehicle for 20 years, twice that if used infrequently. A TW battery with 200 P.P.E. offers limited power (roughly 20 hours of constant use), or the vehicle can be set up to function four hours every time the pilot (or someone) pumps 10 P.P.E. (or 20 I.S.P.) into it. Built-in P.P.E. Battery: Optional for an additional cost of 225,000 credits, a built-in TW P.P.E. Battery holding a reserve of 100 P.P.E. can be added. This is enough for an additional 20 hours of drive time, but is seldom purchased unless TW Features are added; the Dune Buggy doesn''t usually come with TW features. [sic: Dune Buggy is printed in the Sand Ranger entry] A true all-purpose vehicle, the A.W.M. production of the Sand Ranger comes equipped with several weapon systems to supplement its role as a workhorse. Techno-Wizard Features: None standard, other than the power system. As many as three TW features may be added for an additional cost, but most people don''t bother. Half of the Sand Rangers in the A.M.C. have the TW Force Field (80 M.D.C.) and the P.P.E. Battery to power it.', 'Rifts World Book 28: Arzno - Vampire Incursion p.108-109');

